<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 9 October, from 1238 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1238">1238 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">788 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James I of Aragon enters the city of Valencia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After defeating the Moors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> of Balansiya, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> entered the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, an event regarded as the dawn of the Kingdom of Valencia, a component realm of the Crown of Aragon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1446">1446 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">580 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Sejong promulgates the Korean alphabet</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejong-the-great">Sejong the Great</a> of Joseon published the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunminjeongeum">Hunminjeongeum</a>, introducing a new phonetic script now called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangul">Hangul</a>. Designed so ordinary people could read and write, it is commemorated each year on Hangul Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1531">1531 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Catholic cantons declare war on Protestant Zürich</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pressed by a food embargo, the five Catholic cantons of Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> declared war on the Protestant canton of Zürich, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-kappel">Second War of Kappel</a>. On 11 October they defeated Zürich at Kappel, where the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli">Huldrych Zwingli</a> was killed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kappel">Battle of Kappel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/connecticut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1701">1701 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">325 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Connecticut charters the school that became Yale</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> General Assembly chartered the Collegiate School to train ministers and public leaders. It later settled in New Haven and in 1718 was renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yale-university">Yale College</a> after the benefactor Elihu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ial">Yale</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1708">1708 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">318 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter I of Russia defeats a Swedish convoy at Lesnaya</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, Peter I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> caught a Swedish convoy under General Adam Ludwig Lewenhaupt at Lesnaya, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, and defeated it. The convoy was carrying reinforcements and supplies to the main Swedish army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1874">1874 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">152 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Bern founds the Universal Postal Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Representatives of 22 countries signed the Treaty of Bern, creating a single postal territory for exchanging letters. Its anniversary is marked as World Post Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon is born in Liverpool</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Winston Lennon was born at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liverpool">Liverpool</a> Maternity Hospital. As co-founder and songwriter of the Beatles, and later as a solo artist and peace campaigner, he became one of the defining figures of 20th-century popular culture.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Uganda gains independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Uganda became independent with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> as prime minister and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabaka-of-buganda">Kabaka of Buganda</a> later as president. Its early decades were marked by political upheaval, including the dictatorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
